-- Deliverable D §9.2, the worked example, with the label-match bug already fixed:
-- `Q5 CONTAINS Q5.Apple`, never `Q5 CONTAINS "apple"` (D §9.1 — labels are translated, so
-- matching on them breaks in every non-base language).
IF Q5 CONTAINS Q5.Apple
   AND Q6 > 10
   AND ( S1 = 1
         OR ( COUNT(Q5) >= 3 AND Q5 NONE OF [99] ) )
   AND NOT (AGE < 18)
  THEN SHOW Q12
   AND SET HEAVY_BUYER = TRUE
  ELSE HIDE Q12
